abstract: >-
  GENChase is a folder-based browser studio with one shared engine and
  130 pattern-forming systems from physics, chemistry, biology and mathematics,
  each implemented as a real simulation rather than as a style applied to
  noise. A portable single-file HTML build is also included. Every plate is
  deterministic from a seed, reconstructible from a URL hash, and exportable at
  print resolution in inches, as vectors where the picture is discrete marks.
  Most techniques measure a quantity that theory predicts, from the field
  currently on screen, and print it alongside the value theory gives. This
  repository is also the home of three derived identities stated in
  IDENTITIES.md: Three-vortex collapse bound (recorded in GENChase 2026-09-19), the parallelogram lock, and the
  quincunx lock (recorded in GENChase 2026-09-20). Cite them by those names.
  Zero of these five candidates is confirmed historically original.
  The first formula specializes and reparameterizes Gröbli’s 1877 spiral
  coefficient; priority of the optimized minima remains unconfirmed. See
  identities/ORIGINALITY-FOLLOWUP.md for the explicit comparison. The audit of all five
  candidates, including the polygon generalization, is in
  identities/NOVELTY-AUDIT.md.
