references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Three-vortex collapse bound: an explicit formula and sharp minimum for a classical three-vortex collapse family"
    authors:
      - name: "Chaos"
        website: "https://github.com/SharpMeow"
    year: 2026
    month: 9
    url: "https://github.com/SharpMeow/GENChase/blob/main/IDENTITIES.md"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/SharpMeow/GENChase"
    abstract: >-
      Three point vortices with circulations (1, 1, -1/2) on the L=0 circle
      collapse self-similarly. Their dimensionless product of initial angular
      velocity and collapse time is omega_0 t_c = (2 - cos^2 theta) / sin(2 theta)
      >= sqrt(2), with equality uniquely at tan theta = 1/sqrt(2), a triangle
      of interior angles 22.5, 45, and 112.5 degrees. Independently derived
      in GENChase with AI assistance and recorded here 2026-09-19. The formula
      specializes Gröbli’s 1877 spiral coefficient; priority of the optimized
      minimum remains unconfirmed. See identities/ORIGINALITY-FOLLOWUP.md.
      This descriptive title makes no claim of historical priority.
    keywords:
      - Three-vortex collapse bound
      - point vortex
      - self-similar collapse
      - Gröbli
      - Aref
  - type: generic
    title: "Parallelogram lock: an explicit formula and sharp minimum for the Novikov–Sedov four-vortex parallelogram collapse"
    authors:
      - name: "Chaos"
        website: "https://github.com/SharpMeow"
    year: 2026
    month: 9
    url: "https://github.com/SharpMeow/GENChase/blob/main/IDENTITIES.md"
    notes: "Recorded in GENChase 2026-09-20. omega_0 t_c >= 3 sqrt(5)/4 at cos 2theta = 1/4."
  - type: generic
    title: "Quincunx lock: an explicit formula and sharp minimum for the Novikov–Sedov five-vortex quincunx collapse"
    authors:
